1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,128
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:13,638
<i>Frankly, I don't care</i>
<i>if your mother's dead.</i>

3
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:15,098
<i>And besides, you know? She deserves it.</i>

4
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:16,307
<i>Your mom was a slut.</i>

5
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:17,809
[Julio] <i>Didn't it cross your mind</i>

6
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:20,186
<i>you could've gotten yourself</i>
<i>killed doing this?</i>

7
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:21,604
[Diego] <i>I'm not afraid to die.</i>

8
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:24,315
-[Julio] <i>Then I won't kill you just yet.</i>
<i>-Papa!</i>

9
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:28,069
[Julio] <i>I'll make you feel just</i>
<i>how much you deserve to suffer.</i>

10
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:30,155
[Carlotta] <i>She will find a way to give</i>

11
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:33,575
<i>her family the justice they deserve.</i>

12
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:35,952
<i>If you're going to fight the Ardientes,</i>

13
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,621
<i>then I won't let you go alone.</i>
<i>I'll fight with you.</i>

14
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:42,083
[Loring] <i>How could you let this</i>
<i>happen to your son?!</i>

15
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,543
[Diego] <i>I want to find my relatives.</i>

16
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:45,712
<i>My biological relatives.</i>

17
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:47,881
[Loring] <i>That's Rosario. Your mother.</i>

18
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,924
[Ivy] <i>We need them, Mom.</i>

19
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:53,887
<i>All three of them will testify</i>
<i>against the Ardientes</i>

20
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:58,058
<i>Ivy, we have the same goal now.</i>
<i>Let's take them to court.</i>

21
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:00,351
<i>The right punishment for the Ardientes</i>

22
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:02,353
<i>isn't written in the law.</i>

23
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:04,689
[Fernan] <i>Diego and I saw the congressman.</i>

24
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:07,525
<i>He's running the gambling den</i>
<i>in this town.</i>

25
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,195
<i>We'll form a group. We'll take back</i>

26
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:13,865
<i>from the Ardientes what's rightfully ours.</i>

27
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,950
[reporter] <i>Attorney, what</i>
<i>can you say to the Ardientes?</i>

28
00:01:16,284 --> 00:01:17,577
[Georgina] <i>We're coming for all of you.</i>

29
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,162
[Emilia] <i>Who's behind this?</i>

30
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:20,288
<i>Camia Cruz.</i>

31
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:21,539
[Nimfa] <i>Diego, it's Dad.</i>

32
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:24,417
<i>I heard they're going to attack</i>
<i>the congressman's gambling den!</i>

33
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,960
<i>No one else should know about this.</i>

34
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:27,378
<i>If the Ardientes find out</i>
<i>that Mister Fernan</i>

35
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,588
<i>is going against them,</i>

36
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:30,465
<i>your father's life will be at risk.</i>

37
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,675
<i>But, don't worry. I'll go after them.</i>

38
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:36,721
[grunting]

39
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:40,809
[tense music playing]

40
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:44,062
[grunting]

41
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:49,109
[indistinct shouting]

42
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:52,112
[indistinct shouting]

43
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,198
[Fernan] Let's go!

44
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:58,952
[Fernan] Stay right here!

45
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:01,412
Look for the others.

46
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:04,374
Where's Mister Dolfo? Look for him!

47
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,251
[Fernan groans]

48
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:08,545
[Diego] Come on. We're almost out of here.

49
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:12,382
[Fernan] Where are the others? Help them.

50
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,509
-[Diego] Hurry up, Fernan.
-[Fernan groans]

51
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:18,471
[Diego] Move it.

52
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:20,723
-[Fernan] Is everybody here?
-[farmer 1] I think so.

53
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:29,440
You can't take this Thursday off.

54
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:31,776
[bodyguard] All right, sir.

55
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:33,987
[Jepoy] Governor.

56
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:35,113
Madrigal.

57
00:02:36,906 --> 00:02:39,075
Why are there so many cars outside?

58
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:40,326
What's the occasion?

59
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,745
Congressman invited the members
of the party list here.

60
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:45,415
Oh. What about me? Didn't he invite me?

61
00:02:46,332 --> 00:02:47,375
I'm afraid not, Governor.

62
00:02:48,751 --> 00:02:50,420
Can I talk to him?

63
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,508
-[Julio] Arnaldo.
-Grandpa.

64
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:58,094
-Are you okay?
-I'm fine.

65
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,597
-Governor.
-[William] Congressman.

66
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,973
It's so nice of you to come.

67
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:03,516
My pleasure, as always.

68
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:06,019
Thank you. Anyway, the--

69
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:08,062
May I please speak with my father?

70
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,522
[William] As you please.

71
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:11,649
-Thank you.
-[Julio] Just a moment.

72
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:21,618
Emilia, what do you want from me?

73
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:24,454
So, you're having a party, Papa.

74
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:28,458
Yes, I am, and obviously,
you're not invited.

75
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,627
Yes, I noticed.

76
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,339
Anyway, Papa,
did you watch the news earlier?

77
00:03:34,422 --> 00:03:36,633
Of course, I'm always watching the news.

78
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:38,218
And?

79
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:40,303
Oh, you want my opinion?

80
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:43,264
Well, if you would ask me…

81
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:46,684
I would prefer that America just bombs

82
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,812
North Korea before they can act.

83
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:52,357
Papa, I'm not talking about that.

84
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,526
I'm talking about the news
of those witnesses

85
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:58,029
accusing us of murder and corruption.

86
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:01,783
Oh, that news. That's what you meant.

87
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:06,621
Well, do you have an idea
who's behind that?

88
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:09,832
Do you think it's Camia Cruz?

89
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,084
[door closes]

90
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:20,593
[instrumental theme music playing]

91
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:33,523
I'm sorry. Did I wake you up?

92
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:35,108
Come here.

93
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:37,944
Why did you come home so late?

94
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:41,322
I was with our lawyer the whole day.

95
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:44,951
I want everything to go according to plan.

96
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:46,577
Have you eaten yet?

97
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:47,996
Yes.

98
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:53,042
You know, earlier, I saw everything on TV.

99
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,838
I thought about your father.

100
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:59,007
You probably don't know about it,

101
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:02,677
but he went up against
powerful people too.

102
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,263
He didn't back down from anything.

103
00:05:05,596 --> 00:05:07,557
He wasn't scared of death threats,

104
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:11,269
and he wanted to right every wrong.

105
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,564
He would fight for it until the end.

106
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,609
You really took after him, Lily.

107
00:05:20,611 --> 00:05:22,905
I guess I really did, Mom.

108
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:28,411
Since everything I'm doing now
is for our family.

109
00:05:30,413 --> 00:05:31,622
Come here.

110
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,589
[Julio] I did a background check.

111
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:46,262
Camia Cruz is a former
public school teacher.

112
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:49,348
You wanted to kill her out of jealousy.

113
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,185
Now, you're telling me

114
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:57,065
I should worry about
a public school teacher?

115
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:03,696
You know, Emilia,
if Camia Cruz is still alive…

116
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:06,282
she's not a threat to me.

117
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:11,496
Although she is a threat to you.

118
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:19,295
Your unfaithful husband
will cheat on you yet again.

119
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,505
I'm telling you.

120
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:22,673
Keep an eye on him.

121
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:24,300
[Julio chuckles]

122
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:30,807
[Julio]<i> ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

123
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,476
[all] <i>♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

124
00:06:33,559 --> 00:06:36,854
<i>♪ Happy birthday ♪</i>

125
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:41,859
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

126
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,237
-[Julio] Cheers, everyone!
-[clapping]

127
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,988
A round of applause!

128
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,491
[Diego] We're almost there.

129
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:52,703
[Fernan groaning]

130
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,500
Diego, thank you.

131
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:01,295
If it wasn't for you,
I would've been dead by now.

132
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:03,881
Mister Fernan, violence isn't the answer.

133
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,341
What's gotten into you?

134
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:09,804
I get that, Diego.
But, you can't stop me now.

135
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,265
[Fernan] We have the same goal,

136
00:07:12,598 --> 00:07:14,559
but different perspectives.

137
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:20,523
I just hope the day will come
when we'll work together

138
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:21,858
to fight against the Ardientes.

139
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:25,611
[groans]

140
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:30,867
Everyone, get some rest.
Some of you should come with me

141
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:34,287
so we can buy some things
we can give to the people.

142
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,872
Mike, get the bag.

143
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:40,209
[tense music playing]

144
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:49,510
[man] Congressman, a group of bandits

145
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:50,678
robbed the gambling den.

146
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:55,266
Seven of my men were injured.
We lost about 100,000 pesos.

147
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,311
Everyone knows you're
the gambling lord here.

148
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:01,689
Whoever did this has no respect for you.

149
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:04,400
They're not afraid of you.

150
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:11,782
Tell your men that I'm putting
up a 100,000-peso reward…

151
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:18,122
for every bandit they catch.

152
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:20,666
[Julio] They have nothing to worry about.

153
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:23,711
They will be rewarded with money…

154
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:28,424
whether they catch them dead or alive.

155
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,765
[line rings]

156
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:37,934
Yes, I'm looking for

157
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:41,646
Atty. Georgina Fisher.
I just want to ask something.

158
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,105
[woman over the phone] <i>About what, sir?</i>

159
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:44,565
Uh…

160
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:47,485
About the exposé that was aired earlier.

161
00:08:47,735 --> 00:08:49,862
Is Camia Cruz your client?

162
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,489
Are you a reporter?

163
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:55,326
I'm afraid not, but I'm her boyfriend.

164
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:59,080
Uh, I just want to know where she is, and…

165
00:08:59,163 --> 00:09:01,541
Hello? Hello?

166
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:05,503
Boyfriend?

167
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:13,052
Emilia. Camia is alive.

168
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:16,514
And when we see each other
again, I'm choosing her.

169
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:22,311
If that happens, she'll wish
she died in the fire.

170
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:26,357
And if you hurt Camia again,
I'll kill you myself.

171
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:35,116
[Fernan] Everyone, please fall in line!

172
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:37,243
Please don't push each other.

173
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:40,830
We'll make sure that each
and every one of you

174
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:46,043
will get food, bread,
and most importantly, money.

175
00:09:46,627 --> 00:09:48,379
These goods are all for you.

176
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:54,468
We're just giving back what the
Ardientes have stolen from you.

177
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,137
[farmer 1] One at a time, everyone.

178
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,513
[Fernan] Please fall in line.

179
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,599
[Fernan] Come here.
Get your goods over here.

180
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:01,684
-[farmer 2] Here.
-[farmer 1] Ma'am, here you go.

181
00:10:02,226 --> 00:10:03,603
[birds chirping]

182
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:08,107
[tense music playing]

183
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:11,444
Dress up, you two. We're going somewhere.

184
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:13,195
Where to, Papa?

185
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:17,283
We'll attend Governor
Alvarez's charity event.

186
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:21,454
We'll face the public and let them know

187
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:27,001
that we are one big happy
and loving family.

188
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:30,296
We'll also show them…

189
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:33,549
we aren't affected by those allegations

190
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,634
being thrown at us.

191
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:40,681
Because we are not guilty!

192
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:44,477
[Julio] Hey, Raul!

193
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:48,064
Don't you sneer at me like that!

194
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:50,191
I'm still talking to you two.

195
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:54,070
And also, don't forget
to wear something nice.

196
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:59,116
Why don't you take a bath?

197
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:06,666
[William] Look, they're here!

198
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:17,927
[reporter 1] Congressman!

199
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,470
[reporter 2] Congressman!

200
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:20,805
[reporter 3] Could you give a comment?

201
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:21,639
[Julio] Governor.

202
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:23,099
[William] Congressman, how are you?

203
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:24,266
[Julio] I'm fine, thanks.

204
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,309
[William] This way, please.

205
00:11:25,393 --> 00:11:28,604
[reporter 1] Congressman!
What can you say about…

206
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:31,315
-[Ivy] It looks good on you.
-[Carlotta] Ivy!

207
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:35,069
<i>We're live here in Poblacion Ardiente,</i>

208
00:11:35,152 --> 00:11:37,405
<i>where the Ardientes will make</i>
<i>their first public appearance</i>

209
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:41,826
<i>since the exposé about the crimes</i>
<i>they allegedly committed was aired.</i>

210
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,203
<i>What can you say about</i>
<i>those accusations against you?</i>

211
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:46,747
[Emilia] <i>My dear friends…</i>

212
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,041
I'm sorry, but we have no comment on that.

213
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:52,128
We're here for Governor
Alvarez's charity event.

214
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:54,839
We're here to help our constituents.

215
00:11:54,922 --> 00:11:57,091
Is there any truth
to the allegations against you?

216
00:11:58,426 --> 00:12:00,052
<i>I'm afraid we can't comment.</i>

217
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,596
<i>Our lawyers will take care of this,</i>
<i>okay? I'm really sorry.</i>

218
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:06,183
[reporter] <i>Congressman, could you please</i>
<i>give a statement to your loyal supporters?</i>

219
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,815
[Julio] <i>I'm sorry.</i>

220
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:16,944
I guess it's true that you
become more emotional

221
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:18,320
when you grow older.

222
00:12:18,404 --> 00:12:19,697
Why are you getting emotional,
Congressman?

223
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,657
[reporter] <i>Yes, Congressman?</i>

224
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,118
<i>It's very difficult for a father…</i>

225
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:27,746
to see and hear someone
discredit his loved ones…

226
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:32,042
and tarnish his family's name.

227
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,962
I'm sure you know this already.

228
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:39,758
Ever since the beginning,
the core values I've taught my children

229
00:12:40,426 --> 00:12:44,305
are excellence, honesty, and integrity.

230
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:48,601
[Julio] <i>Despite all this,</i>
<i>I believe we can get through</i>

231
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:50,394
this trying time.

232
00:12:51,437 --> 00:12:55,441
Rest assured that we Ardientes
will continue

233
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:59,236
serving our constituents
in Poblacion Ardiente.

234
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,447
-[man] Liar! Murderer!
-[security 1] Who said that?

235
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:03,032
You shameless thieves!

236
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:04,825
[woman 2] We don't believe you anymore!

237
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,203
-Get out of here!
-Ouch!

238
00:13:07,286 --> 00:13:09,580
[indistinct shouting]

239
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:10,789
Get out of here!

240
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:13,459
[security 2] Stop that! Stop that!

241
00:13:14,835 --> 00:13:18,631
[woman] <i>Get out of here, murderers!</i>
<i>Leave our town!</i>

242
00:13:18,714 --> 00:13:20,758
[townsfolk clamoring]

243
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:23,844
-[Jepoy] Stop it already!
-[woman] Liars!

244
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,012
[Emilia] Calm down, everyone!

245
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,096
[woman] <i>Get out of here!</i>

246
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,641
<i>-Get them out of here!</i>
<i>-Get out of here!</i>

247
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:30,267
Get them out of here!

248
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:32,561
They don't have a permit to hold a rally.

249
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:35,105
[man] You! You're a worthless governor!

250
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,690
You're just the Ardientes' lapdog!

251
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:38,234
[Emilia] That's enough. Calm down…

252
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:39,818
<i>…friends. Listen!</i>

253
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:42,613
[Emilia] <i>Violence will</i>
<i>never solve anything.</i>

254
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:44,615
-Let's stop this.
-[woman] You're a liar!

255
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,784
-[security 5] Hey!
-[security 6] Show some respect!

256
00:13:46,867 --> 00:13:48,786
[security 7] Show some respect!

257
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:50,746
[indistinct shouting]

258
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:53,958
[Emilia] <i>Friends! That's enough, everyone!</i>

259
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:55,668
-[indistinct shouting]
<i>-You!</i>

260
00:13:55,751 --> 00:14:00,422
<i>Whoever's spreading rumors</i>
<i>about our family, come out!</i>

261
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:01,674
<i>Face us!</i>

262
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:04,969
[tense music playing]

263
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:10,099
-Down with the Ardientes!
-Down with the Ardientes!

264
00:14:10,182 --> 00:14:13,894
[crowd chanting] <i>Down with the Ardientes!</i>

265
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:17,898
Down with the Ardientes!
Down with the Ardientes!

266
00:14:17,982 --> 00:14:19,567
Down with the Ardientes!

267
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:23,612
Down with the Ardientes!
Down with the Ardientes!

268
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:27,408
-[crowd continues chanting]
-[indistinct shouting]

269
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:30,744
[tense music playing]

270
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:37,126
[chuckles]

271
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:42,006
Did you see that?
The people are all furious now.

272
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:45,676
They're aware of how cruel
the Ardientes are.

273
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:52,850
I swear, Mom, this is only
the beginning of our battle

274
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:54,268
against the Ardientes.

275
00:14:55,519 --> 00:15:01,191
I promise you, I'll make
sure they won't win this fight.

276
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:07,656
And every person they've wronged
will fight with us.

277
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:10,200
This is what I'll do.

278
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:16,749
I'll look for all
the victims Julio, Emilia,

279
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:20,377
and Raul have wronged.
I will talk to all of them

280
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:25,799
and urge them to file lawsuits
against the Ardientes.

281
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:28,761
Mom, this is it. What we've waited for.

282
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:32,806
We can finally have the justice
we want for Dad,

283
00:15:32,890 --> 00:15:35,726
for what they did to you
and to our family.

284
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:40,105
The Ardientes are going down, Mom.

285
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,819
[Loring] They're lucky they
only got tomatoes.

286
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:49,657
Considering what they did,
they should be locked up.

287
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:55,287
I've experienced their cruelty, firsthand.

288
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,333
Let me ask you, Diego.

289
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,169
Who do you think is behind all this?

290
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:07,049
<i>The right punishment for the Ardientes</i>

291
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,801
<i>isn't written in the law.</i>

292
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:13,681
<i>So I'll take it into my own</i>
<i>hands and deal with them myself.</i>

293
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:20,312
Whoever it is, we should be thanking them.

294
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:25,067
The Ardientes won't stop
until they're dealt with.

295
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:31,657
They have the guts to go against
the Ardientes. It's inspiring.

296
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:34,994
Like what Fernan's group is doing.

297
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:39,123
[ominous music playing]

298
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:45,462
Mom, I've been thinking about
joining Mister Fernan's cause.

299
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:48,298
We'll get the cooperative
back from the Ardientes.

300
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:57,766
-We can fix this, Congressman.
-And how exactly do we do that?

301
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,644
What happened there?
What stupidity was that?

302
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:02,521
I thought you had a handle
on the charity event?

303
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:05,733
How did the press get in there?

304
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:09,153
And you even let those people
humiliate us in public!

305
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:10,738
You failed to protect us.

306
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:14,158
That alone is enough for me
not to trust you!

307
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:17,077
-But, Congressman--
-[Julio] Shut up!

308
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,163
Shut up and just leave, William.

309
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:25,002
And I better not hear any comment from you

310
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:28,338
regarding this issue. Now, get out.

311
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:31,383
Don't make me regret giving you
your position in office

312
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:34,011
and strip it from you.

313
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,848
Go and leave me!

314
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:59,745
If you were there with me, Arnaldo,

315
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,580
that wouldn't have happened.

316
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:04,583
I'm sorry.
I should've been there with you.

317
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:06,335
It's not your fault.

318
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:09,505
You had important business
at the city hall.

319
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:12,132
But what happened validates you

320
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:16,845
as my choice to take over
Poblacion Ardiente after me.

321
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:20,682
How can I trust someone like Alvarez?

322
00:18:21,391 --> 00:18:24,603
All the while I thought
he was smart and quiet,

323
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:27,356
but he turned out
to be dumb and talkative.

324
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:29,191
To tell you the truth,

325
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:33,195
I'd actually choose your mother over him.

326
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:36,156
Of course. You trained Mom

327
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,533
-yourself, so--
-[Julio] Yes.

328
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:40,619
Until she threw it all away

329
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:44,456
when she bit the hand
that was giving her everything.

330
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:48,460
[Julio sighs]

331
00:18:53,048 --> 00:18:54,424
[Emilia] In times like these,

332
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:57,219
one has to be
a sneak to get the best stuff.

333
00:18:57,302 --> 00:18:58,428
[Claire chuckles softly]

334
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:03,392
Careful. Your Papa might find out

335
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:05,978
you're stealing from
his collection of vintage wines.

336
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,147
Aunt Claire, at the rate things are going,

337
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:10,023
I don't think he'll notice.

338
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:13,152
That's his karma
for banishing his only child.

339
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:14,611
Thank you.

340
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:19,867
Well Raul, let's toast to Papa's downfall.

341
00:19:19,950 --> 00:19:21,410
[Claire] Madrigal, can I have
some, please?

342
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,580
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

343
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,582
[Claire] You know what?

344
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,542
I like what you did earlier.

345
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,420
You challenged Camia Cruz to come out.

346
00:19:31,503 --> 00:19:32,963
That was very bold.

347
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:34,631
[scoffs]

348
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:37,092
[Claire] Do you really think
she's behind all this?

349
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:42,264
If it really is her,
I don't think she'll come out.

350
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,142
The truth is, she's scared.

351
00:19:45,809 --> 00:19:49,730
You know what bothers me,
Auntie? That Attorney Fisher.

352
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,482
There's definitely something
"fishy" about her.

353
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:54,651
But you know what? I did some research.

354
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:57,154
She's a big-time lawyer.

355
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:02,826
If it's true that Raul
locked up Camia for a long time,

356
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:07,831
I believe she's not
the only one behind this.

357
00:20:08,123 --> 00:20:10,375
Someone big is backing her up.

358
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,295
Natalie?

359
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,297
She could've found out

360
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:17,174
you're the one who had her father killed.

361
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,175
[chuckles]

362
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,677
Auntie, I don't think she's bold enough.

363
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:25,557
I think it's someone
who has a grudge against our family.

364
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,727
Or someone who's very close to Camia Cruz.

365
00:20:29,394 --> 00:20:31,647
[tense music playing]

366
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,357
Who could that be?

367
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:36,318
Could it be her darned daughter?

368
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:41,615
[Julio] Well, of course, my friend.

369
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:45,494
Well, clearly, this is
propaganda from our critics.

370
00:20:45,869 --> 00:20:48,497
These are but false accusations.

371
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:55,128
Anyway, thank you for calling.
This issue will soon die down.

372
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:01,843
That Camia Cruz is becoming a problem.

373
00:21:02,844 --> 00:21:03,929
Is she even real?

374
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:08,308
She <i>is</i> real.

375
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:12,896
And I can't deny that she's a threat.

376
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:19,486
But, obviously, she's not alone.
Someone's backing her up.

377
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:22,114
Then, who? Dad?

378
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,824
I don't think so.

379
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:28,495
No one in this household
would have the guts to do that.

380
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:31,081
They know I'm watching them like a hawk.

381
00:21:32,082 --> 00:21:33,917
Do you know who I'm suspecting?

382
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:38,005
Miss Aguas.

383
00:21:39,673 --> 00:21:41,633
[Emilia] You know, Auntie,
she could be alive.

384
00:21:42,134 --> 00:21:45,178
Raul, what's the name of Diego's
best friend again?

385
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:52,602
I have to go out.

386
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,647
Madrigal, go with him.

387
00:21:58,358 --> 00:21:59,776
[Emilia] You know, Auntie, at this point,

388
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:03,822
I don't really care
who's backing Camia Cruz.

389
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:08,535
My concern right now is how
to regain my old position.

390
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:11,913
The weaker Papa gets…

391
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:16,126
the bigger the chances of
taking him down are.

392
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,046
Good thinking.

393
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:25,093
[Julio] This all happened
while she wasn't in Ardiente.

394
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:28,847
[Julio sighs]

395
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:34,561
I don't get it. What does Ivy
have to do with Camia Cruz?

396
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:38,607
That is another thing
that we need to know.

397
00:22:39,107 --> 00:22:42,944
And we also need to silence…

398
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:48,867
or twist the testimonies against us.

399
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:51,912
And more importantly, we need to know

400
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:55,707
where our enemies
are hiding those witnesses.

401
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:58,543
Okay, Grandpa. I'll handle it.

402
00:22:58,627 --> 00:23:00,087
Do it as soon as possible.

403
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:04,007
We can't give them a chance
to file a case against us.

404
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:10,680
Ivy Aguas.

405
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,392
[Ivy] Very good, Attorney.

406
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:16,144
Our plan was a success.

407
00:23:16,645 --> 00:23:19,439
Thank you, Miss Aguas.
I will file the criminal cases

408
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:21,274
against the Ardientes right away.

409
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:26,071
Okay. I'll send the media
to cover the case filing.

410
00:23:26,154 --> 00:23:29,533
I want to bombard the Ardientes
with propaganda.

411
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:33,662
And before you leave,
I want you to do another thing.

412
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:36,957
Visit all the families listed there.

413
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:41,878
Convince each of them to testify
against the Ardientes.

414
00:23:41,962 --> 00:23:43,380
The more families we have,

415
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:45,340
the more compelling our case will be.

416
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,509
This is very exciting, Miss Aguas.

417
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:50,637
Let's see if Julio's lawyers

418
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:54,558
can handle all the cases
we'll file against them.

419
00:23:57,727 --> 00:23:59,980
[Fernan] Diego, thank you for helping us.

420
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:02,482
Mister Fernan, the cooperative
is important to all of us.

421
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:04,025
Most of us depend on it.

422
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:07,445
If we get it back,
we can start over again.

423
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:08,655
You're right.

424
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:17,706
Everyone, Mister Fernan,
can you please excuse us?

425
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:20,375
[Fernan] Okay. Everyone, let's go inside.

426
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:27,215
[tense music playing]

427
00:24:28,175 --> 00:24:29,676
Dad, what are you doing here?

428
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:34,973
[Raul] I'm sorry for
interrupting your conversation.

429
00:24:35,056 --> 00:24:37,851
I just want to ask you something.

430
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:44,357
Uh… Do you remember Lily Cruz,
your childhood friend?

431
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:48,612
Do you know anything about her?
Is she still alive?

432
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:52,699
[tense music swells]

433
00:24:52,782 --> 00:24:53,700
I don't know.

434
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:57,746
I haven't heard anything
about her since she left.

435
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:00,248
Why do you ask?

436
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:05,754
I was thinking that Lily
might've found Camia first.

437
00:25:06,421 --> 00:25:08,089
They might be together right now.

438
00:25:08,173 --> 00:25:13,261
And they're both taking revenge
on Julio and Emilia.

439
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:17,057
I don't know, Dad.

440
00:25:20,185 --> 00:25:21,102
[Raul] I'm sorry.

441
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:26,107
I just wanted to know how Camia was doing.

442
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:33,698
I hope she's fine, happy,
and safe. That's all.

443
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:38,119
Don't worry. We might not know
how Camia is,

444
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:42,207
but I'm sure they're about to get justice

445
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:45,585
for everything the Ardientes
put them through.

446
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:49,422
But I hope you know, Dad,

447
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:51,675
that they won't be
the only ones to pay for it.

448
00:25:53,009 --> 00:25:56,638
You're guilty too. You were
their accomplice in everything.

449
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:05,146
Go back to the mansion, Dad.
You might get in trouble again.

450
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:08,858
Diego, son.

451
00:26:10,694 --> 00:26:11,695
Forgive me.

452
00:26:15,573 --> 00:26:16,950
I didn't want all this.

453
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:21,913
Take care of yourself.

454
00:26:21,997 --> 00:26:26,543
[tense music playing]

455
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:40,682
Lily.

456
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:45,562
I was thinking that we could
have a stronger case if I--

457
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,604
Mom.

458
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,775
I don't agree.

459
00:26:51,234 --> 00:26:53,194
But, Lily, this all started because of me.

460
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:55,322
Mom, I won't allow it.

461
00:26:55,405 --> 00:26:59,659
I won't give them the chance
to ruin and tear us apart again.

462
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:03,246
Yes, I want us to face them together,

463
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:07,167
but I won't let any of us be hurt again.

464
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:11,254
Mom, I know what you feel.
I know you want to help.

465
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:13,006
Thank you, Mom.

466
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:16,092
But I want you to trust in my plans.

467
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:19,554
I assure you no one will get hurt.

468
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:21,890
And like I promised you,

469
00:27:21,973 --> 00:27:25,435
those good-for-nothing Ardientes
will get what they deserve.

470
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:30,732
[tense music playing]

471
00:27:36,738 --> 00:27:37,906
[goon 1] Let's have a drink, man.

472
00:27:38,114 --> 00:27:40,617
[goon 2] Okay. I've been waiting
for you to say that.

473
00:27:44,037 --> 00:27:46,748
[goon 2] Nice and cold!
Just the way I like it.

474
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:50,001
[goon 1] Why did our boss
make us guard this place?

475
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:52,253
Forget that. At least we have a job!

476
00:27:52,796 --> 00:27:53,797
[goon 1] I'm going to pee.

477
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:58,635
[whispering] One. Two. Three.

478
00:27:58,718 --> 00:27:59,928
Feels good.

479
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:02,180
-[goon 1] Hey!
-[grunts]

480
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:05,725
[Diego] That's enough! That's enough! Hey!

481
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:07,185
All right. Tie them up.

482
00:28:08,645 --> 00:28:10,021
[Fernan] What should we do with them?

483
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:11,773
Just set them aside, Mister Fernan.

484
00:28:11,856 --> 00:28:13,233
[Diego] We'll use them for later.

485
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:14,651
Okay, Mister Fernan.

486
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:16,319
Where's the key?

487
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:17,570
[goon 2] We don't have it.

488
00:28:17,654 --> 00:28:19,739
-Where's the key?!
-[farmer] Give us the key!

489
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,533
-We don't have it.
-Do you want me to hit you?!

490
00:28:21,616 --> 00:28:22,492
Just hand it over!

491
00:28:22,575 --> 00:28:25,453
[Diego] Mister Danny,
where's the hammer? Move aside.

492
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:27,789
[goon 1] Hey! Don't do that!

493
00:28:33,586 --> 00:28:34,879
[farmer 3] We're taking this back now!

494
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,756
-[farmer 1] Yes!
-[farmers cheering]

495
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:38,133
[Fernan] We did it!

496
00:28:38,883 --> 00:28:42,095
[indistinct chatter]

497
00:28:43,888 --> 00:28:46,391
Attorney, have you filed a case
against the Ardientes yet?

498
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:48,727
Yes, we filed multiple counts of murder

499
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:50,562
and a number of corruption cases

500
00:28:50,645 --> 00:28:54,274
against Congressman Julio
Ardiente, Emilia Torillo,

501
00:28:54,357 --> 00:28:56,276
Raul Torillo, and Arnaldo Torillo.

502
00:28:56,359 --> 00:28:58,278
Do you have a message for the Ardientes?

503
00:28:58,486 --> 00:28:59,779
I'm coming for all of you.

504
00:29:02,031 --> 00:29:06,619
[Ivy] <i>I won't stop as long as</i>
<i>there's an Ardiente in power</i>

505
00:29:06,995 --> 00:29:10,331
<i>with the freedom to do what they want.</i>

506
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:14,836
<i>I'll make sure all of them</i>
<i>will rot in prison.</i>

507
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:18,548
Attorney Georgina.

508
00:29:19,883 --> 00:29:22,427
You're a woman of your word.
You work really fast.

509
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:24,971
I'm not only fast. I'm also good.

510
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:28,892
I know, I know. Too bad you'll be…

511
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:31,978
using your skills for something
you'll regret later on.

512
00:29:32,061 --> 00:29:35,607
[chuckles] Are you threatening
me, Mr. Ardiente?

513
00:29:35,690 --> 00:29:36,608
You know, it's been a while

514
00:29:36,691 --> 00:29:39,402
since someone called me "Mister".

515
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:41,946
Because you don't deserve
to be called "Congressman".

516
00:29:42,030 --> 00:29:42,947
Ouch!

517
00:29:43,031 --> 00:29:45,700
You are a dirty politician,
and I will bring you down.

518
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:50,079
Oh, my! Now, let's not get
ahead of ourselves, attorney.

519
00:29:50,371 --> 00:29:52,040
A lot of things can still happen.

520
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:56,085
Your client, for example.
Camia Cruz, is she?

521
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:57,587
For all you know, she just might

522
00:29:57,670 --> 00:30:00,131
suddenly drop dead even before
the case hearing starts.

523
00:30:00,423 --> 00:30:02,091
Camia Cruz is not my client.

524
00:30:02,175 --> 00:30:05,220
Oh! Who, then? Ivy Aguas?

525
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:06,805
I don't know that woman.

526
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,098
Is she one of your angry mistresses?

527
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:15,188
I like you, Attorney. You're funny.

528
00:30:15,271 --> 00:30:18,608
Such a shame you're playing
for the losing side.

529
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:23,363
Anyway, once I have this case dismissed…

530
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:30,995
I'll get rid of you next.
I will destroy your career.

531
00:30:32,038 --> 00:30:36,876
I will make you regret the day
you decided to take up law.

532
00:30:37,669 --> 00:30:42,173
Bring it on, Mr. Ardiente.
I'm not afraid of you.

533
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:48,054
[blows raspberries]

534
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:52,225
Such a feisty woman!
I'll love a challenge like her.

535
00:30:52,725 --> 00:30:54,310
-[Loring laughing]
-[indistinct chatter]

536
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:55,895
[Loring] Isn't this great?

537
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:57,856
[crowd laughing]

538
00:30:57,939 --> 00:31:02,652
You know, those people
who helped us are real heroes.

539
00:31:02,735 --> 00:31:03,653
True.

540
00:31:03,736 --> 00:31:06,698
And because of these seeds,
we can finally plant again.

541
00:31:06,781 --> 00:31:09,742
[cheering and clapping]

542
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:11,870
Do they work for the Ardientes?

543
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,663
[Fernan] Yes. They do.

544
00:31:13,746 --> 00:31:14,831
[Danny] They were guarding the warehouse.

545
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:16,124
[farmer 5] You're the guy who pushed me!

546
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:18,459
[Loring] People like them
deserve a good beating.

547
00:31:18,543 --> 00:31:20,962
[all cheering]

548
00:31:21,087 --> 00:31:23,172
[indistinct pleading]

549
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:29,679
[farmer 6] Or better yet, why
don't we let the ants bite them?

550
00:31:29,762 --> 00:31:31,639
-[all] Perfect!
-Please don't.

551
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:36,144
[crowd cheering]

552
00:31:36,936 --> 00:31:39,188
[laughing]

553
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:41,566
[farmer 6] I didn't know
they're comedians.

554
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:44,611
So, everyone, what are we waiting for?

555
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:47,196
Let's arrange these goods
so we can start selling them.

556
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,615
-Okay.
-Okay. Game.

557
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:51,284
Okay. Back to work.

558
00:32:00,710 --> 00:32:01,711
[exhales]

559
00:32:03,046 --> 00:32:04,881
What are you doing here, Congressman?

560
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:07,717
Oh.

561
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:12,472
You're the judge handling handle
the case against me, right?

562
00:32:14,974 --> 00:32:18,353
So, do you want it thrown out?

563
00:32:18,853 --> 00:32:20,021
Yes.

564
00:32:21,689 --> 00:32:24,984
Then, you must give the court
compelling evidence

565
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:27,028
that you didn't steal
from the public funds…

566
00:32:27,654 --> 00:32:30,031
and you didn't have anyone killed.

567
00:32:31,407 --> 00:32:32,700
I see.

568
00:32:32,867 --> 00:32:36,245
[tense music playing]

569
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:47,548
Is one million pesos compelling enough?

570
00:32:48,675 --> 00:32:54,847
Oh! And with it, comes a
promotion to the highest court.

571
00:32:55,348 --> 00:32:57,684
I'm sure you'd like that, Judge Rivera,

572
00:32:57,767 --> 00:33:03,856
to be called Justice Rivera
of the Supreme Court.

573
00:33:05,358 --> 00:33:06,943
It's got a nice ring to it.

574
00:33:08,111 --> 00:33:11,656
Are you really this scared
that you need to bribe me?

575
00:33:12,407 --> 00:33:15,535
No. It's not that I'm afraid.

576
00:33:16,035 --> 00:33:21,416
I just want this petty case
dismissed as soon as possible.

577
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:23,793
[Judge Alice breathes heavily]

578
00:33:27,547 --> 00:33:29,799
Then I'm sorry, Congressman.

579
00:33:31,259 --> 00:33:33,177
Because you can't buy me.

580
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:37,098
The case will proceed, as usual.

581
00:33:37,223 --> 00:33:39,600
And once we find out you're guilty…

582
00:33:40,309 --> 00:33:42,895
I won't think twice before
unseating you from your position

583
00:33:43,563 --> 00:33:44,689
and locking you up!

584
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:48,026
I see.

585
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:50,153
Well…

586
00:33:50,486 --> 00:33:51,487
[grunts]

587
00:33:54,449 --> 00:33:55,742
You know, it seems like…

588
00:33:56,909 --> 00:34:00,329
everybody has been threatening me lately.

589
00:34:02,165 --> 00:34:06,169
So now it's my turn to give my warning.

590
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:12,842
Julio Ardiente's wrath
is like a hurricane.

591
00:34:14,260 --> 00:34:18,222
It will destroy everything in its path.

592
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:21,517
I'm ready for you, Congressman.

593
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:29,484
[Ivy chuckles]

594
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:32,695
Well, Attorney,
I'm not surprised he said that.

595
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,113
But don't worry.

596
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:38,451
Like the witnesses in this case,
I will protect you.

597
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:40,036
Thank you, Miss Aguas.

598
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:41,537
Oh, by the way…

599
00:34:42,830 --> 00:34:45,583
Julio's under the impression
you're the one behind all this.

600
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:46,667
[chuckles]

601
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:51,547
I know. In fact, I already have
a solution to that problem.

602
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:57,470
But, Lily, aren't you worried

603
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,181
he might have the case dismissed?

604
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:02,934
And what if he turns his attention to you?

605
00:35:03,142 --> 00:35:07,605
Mom, I'm not afraid because we
have solid evidence against him.

606
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:11,734
And the judge handling the case
is on the side of justice.

607
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,362
She can't be bought with money.

608
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:16,572
What about you, Lily?

609
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:21,285
What if Julio finds out that
you're the one behind all this?

610
00:35:21,369 --> 00:35:24,330
Once that happens, I'll face him.

611
00:35:24,413 --> 00:35:28,292
And on the day he gets arrested
to be sent to prison,

612
00:35:28,376 --> 00:35:29,627
I'll be there.

613
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:34,132
I want to see his reaction
when he's put behind bars!

614
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:38,427
[tense music playing]

615
00:35:39,303 --> 00:35:40,429
[crickets chirping]

616
00:35:42,557 --> 00:35:44,559
[tense music swells]

617
00:35:45,184 --> 00:35:46,144
[Atty. Georgina] <i>You don't deserve</i>

618
00:35:46,227 --> 00:35:47,395
<i>to be called "Congressman".</i>

619
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:50,231
<i>You are a dirty politician,</i>
<i>and I will bring you down.</i>

620
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:53,484
<i>You can't buy me. The case will proceed.</i>

621
00:35:53,568 --> 00:35:55,403
<i>And once we find out you're guilty…</i>

622
00:35:55,486 --> 00:35:57,155
<i>I won't think twice before unseating you</i>

623
00:35:57,238 --> 00:35:59,115
<i>from your position and locking you up!</i>

624
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:03,202
I can't understand…

625
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:07,373
why some intelligent people…

626
00:36:09,250 --> 00:36:12,295
become fools because of their principles.

627
00:36:12,378 --> 00:36:15,423
[suspenseful music playing]

628
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,009
[grunts softly]

629
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:20,094
[phone dialing]

630
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:21,304
Hello?

631
00:36:22,054 --> 00:36:24,599
I'm counting on you, my friend.

632
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:26,267
-Don't worry.
-Okay.

633
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,228
Um… I'll see you in the office.

634
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:30,563
-Sure.
-Okay.

635
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:37,778
[suspenseful music playing]

636
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:41,657
[motorcycle engine humming]

637
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:52,251
[suspenseful music swells]

638
00:36:57,924 --> 00:36:59,508
[Judge Alice] Fred, let's go. Hurry.

639
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:06,015
[clinking]

640
00:37:08,851 --> 00:37:12,021
Why did you stop?
I told you to drive faster!

641
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:13,856
Fred, come on!

642
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:18,361
-No!
-[muffled gunshot]

643
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:24,533
[suspenseful music swells]

644
00:37:28,746 --> 00:37:31,791
[motorcycle engine humming]

645
00:37:46,347 --> 00:37:47,932
JUDGE COMMITS SUICIDE

646
00:37:50,434 --> 00:37:51,602
[screams]

647
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:52,812
[Ivy] Suicide?!

648
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:54,730
Who does that
congressman think he's fooling?!

649
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:58,734
I'm sure! I'm very sure he had her killed!

650
00:38:01,862 --> 00:38:03,030
[exhales sharply]

651
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:07,118
Don't worry about it, Mom. We'll
use this against the Ardientes.

652
00:38:07,868 --> 00:38:12,456
Attorney! We'll tell everyone
what really happened.

653
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:14,417
Because the judge didn't commit suicide

654
00:38:14,500 --> 00:38:17,336
but was killed by the Ardientes!

655
00:38:18,045 --> 00:38:19,505
Say that in the press conference!

656
00:38:19,588 --> 00:38:22,675
That's what I want you to do. Now!

657
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:31,934
They can fool everyone, but not me! Never.

658
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:41,944
Thank you for the promotion, Señor Julio.

659
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:44,739
I've always wanted to be an RTC judge.

660
00:38:45,781 --> 00:38:47,366
It's nothing, Vince.

661
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:51,203
After all, your father
and I are very close.

662
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:56,751
Well, now that you're the judge,
you know what to do.

663
00:38:57,793 --> 00:39:00,504
I'll take care of the cases
filed against you.

664
00:39:01,297 --> 00:39:04,175
Good. Very good.

665
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:05,926
[clinks]

666
00:39:09,472 --> 00:39:10,723
JUDGE RIVERA WAS A KNOWN
HUMAN RIGHTS ADVOCATE

667
00:39:10,806 --> 00:39:12,808
HANDLING THE NUMEROUS CASES
AGAINST THE ARDIENTES.

668
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:17,063
<i>I'm sure Ivy's case will be</i>
<i>compromised because of this.</i>

669
00:39:17,146 --> 00:39:18,731
<i>I need to help her.</i>

670
00:39:24,445 --> 00:39:26,739
[Atty. Georgina] This is clearly
an attack on human rights.

671
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:29,950
We do not believe that
Judge Rivera killed herself.

672
00:39:30,242 --> 00:39:33,412
She was killed so that the real
criminals could escape justice.

673
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,790
[reporter] Are you saying that
Congressman Ardiente

674
00:39:35,873 --> 00:39:37,708
ordered Judge Rivera to be killed?

675
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:41,545
We won't stop until the deaths
of these innocent people

676
00:39:41,629 --> 00:39:43,506
are given justice.

677
00:39:44,465 --> 00:39:46,717
[Atty. Georgina] Those who are
drunk with power will pay.

678
00:39:46,801 --> 00:39:50,096
We read that Camia Cruz is one
of the proponents of the case.

679
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:52,348
Where is she?
Why doesn't she show herself?

680
00:39:52,681 --> 00:39:53,974
-Yes, where is she?
-Yes, Attorney.

681
00:39:54,058 --> 00:39:56,936
Where's Camia Cruz?
We want to hear her story.

682
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:00,564
Is someone protecting her?

683
00:40:00,648 --> 00:40:02,149
We need a statement on this, Attorney.

684
00:40:02,817 --> 00:40:04,527
[reporter 3] What is she afraid of?

685
00:40:05,152 --> 00:40:07,113
[reporter 4] Yes, Attorney.
Where is Camia Cruz?

686
00:40:12,368 --> 00:40:14,120
[reporter 2]
<i>We read that Camia Cruz is one</i>

687
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:15,621
<i>of the proponents of the case.</i>

688
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:17,957
<i>Where is she?</i>
<i>Why doesn't she show herself?</i>

689
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:18,958
[reporter 5] <i>Yes, where is she?</i>

690
00:40:19,041 --> 00:40:20,626
[reporter 3] <i>Yes, Attorney.</i>
<i>Where's Camia Cruz?</i>

691
00:40:20,709 --> 00:40:22,503
<i>We want to hear her story.</i>

692
00:40:25,297 --> 00:40:27,049
Miss Aguas, you have a visitor.

693
00:40:29,009 --> 00:40:30,010
Ivy.

694
00:40:30,594 --> 00:40:33,514
Diego, what are you doing here?
Someone might've followed you.

695
00:40:33,597 --> 00:40:36,684
No, Ivy. I'm sure of that.

696
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:39,270
I found out what Grandpa did to the judge.

697
00:40:39,728 --> 00:40:40,813
I want to help you.

698
00:40:43,357 --> 00:40:45,526
Diego, we've already talked about this.

699
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:49,405
Ivy, listen to me. This isn't
just about your parents.

700
00:40:49,905 --> 00:40:51,365
It's about my mother too.

701
00:40:51,824 --> 00:40:54,410
Can't you see we both
have the same goal here?

702
00:40:55,077 --> 00:40:57,663
I wanna do something to prevent
this case from being dismissed.

703
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:01,208
Ivy, you can trust me. I'll help you.

704
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:03,711
Even if I have to testify
against the family

705
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:05,754
who raised me, I'll do it.

706
00:41:06,213 --> 00:41:07,298
[Atty. Georgina] He's right, Ivy.

707
00:41:07,381 --> 00:41:09,258
We need all the help that we can get now.

708
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:11,760
I spoke to the judge earlier,
and he's inclined to dismiss

709
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:13,804
the case if Camia won't show up in court.

710
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:20,769
Hey!

711
00:41:21,562 --> 00:41:23,189
Come, join me.

712
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:24,857
Sit down. Sit down.

713
00:41:25,357 --> 00:41:26,358
Join me.

714
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:29,862
Drink.

715
00:41:30,946 --> 00:41:31,947
Eat.

716
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:34,408
Ha!

717
00:41:35,117 --> 00:41:40,206
Isn't it wonderful to see
my wicked family complete?

718
00:41:40,664 --> 00:41:41,707
[Julio chuckles]

719
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,668
Um, are we celebrating something?

720
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:50,758
Yes, we are celebrating my victory.

721
00:41:52,676 --> 00:41:54,595
Has the case been dismissed, Julio?

722
00:41:56,305 --> 00:41:57,306
Uh…

723
00:41:57,556 --> 00:42:01,644
Well, not yet. But, I'm getting there.

724
00:42:03,729 --> 00:42:08,609
This case will be dismissed
without Camia Cruz

725
00:42:08,692 --> 00:42:09,777
in the picture.

726
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:13,364
And I tell you, it's impossible

727
00:42:13,447 --> 00:42:15,824
for her to show up because she's a coward.

728
00:42:17,034 --> 00:42:19,537
-Ivy, I have to come out.
-Mom, no.

729
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:25,084
Ivy, I didn't get this second
chance just to remain in hiding.

730
00:42:25,668 --> 00:42:27,336
It's about time for me to face them--

731
00:42:27,419 --> 00:42:31,131
No, Mom. It's too dangerous.
I won't let you do this.

732
00:42:31,215 --> 00:42:34,426
Ivy, we can't always live in fear.

733
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:37,012
Because if we do, the Ardientes
will continue holding us

734
00:42:37,096 --> 00:42:38,097
by the scruff of our necks.

735
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:41,225
If other people can
testify in court for this,

736
00:42:41,475 --> 00:42:43,018
I'll do my part too.

737
00:42:43,852 --> 00:42:46,230
Let me do it because this is my fight.

738
00:42:46,313 --> 00:42:47,898
This is our fight.

739
00:42:49,525 --> 00:42:53,946
And if we continue to be afraid,
we can't solve this, Ivy.

740
00:42:56,198 --> 00:42:58,033
Well then, Papa, congratulations!

741
00:42:59,118 --> 00:43:00,202
But, don't you think

742
00:43:00,286 --> 00:43:02,454
the public should know
about our celebration?

743
00:43:04,039 --> 00:43:04,915
What do you mean?

744
00:43:04,999 --> 00:43:06,375
[Emilia] Well Papa, you see,

745
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:10,170
our enemy's tactic is to
humiliate you through the media.

746
00:43:10,546 --> 00:43:13,632
Then why not also celebrate
our victory through the media?

747
00:43:13,716 --> 00:43:15,301
Let's have a grand press conference.

748
00:43:17,136 --> 00:43:19,096
[Claire] Actually, it's the
perfect timing, Julio.

749
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:21,640
Especially now that our enemies are weak.

750
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:34,028
Mom, if that's what you want.

751
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:38,157
If you're going to face them,
then I will too.

752
00:43:38,741 --> 00:43:40,242
Let's do it together.

753
00:43:41,535 --> 00:43:45,664
Ivy, no. I'm the only one
who'll come out in the open.

754
00:43:46,457 --> 00:43:48,584
Because you have to continue our fight

755
00:43:48,667 --> 00:43:50,836
if something happens to me.

756
00:43:50,919 --> 00:43:56,175
I won't let you do that, Mom.
Just like what I promised you,

757
00:43:56,300 --> 00:44:00,179
I'll protect you from the Ardientes!

758
00:44:01,513 --> 00:44:05,059
We will fight, Mom. The two of us.

759
00:44:05,142 --> 00:44:09,897
[tense music playing]

760
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:19,698
[Julio] You know, this
family could have been

761
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:23,619
much more powerful
if we only worked together.

762
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:26,872
If you didn't go against me before…

763
00:44:27,456 --> 00:44:30,959
our enemies wouldn't have seen
the chink in our armor.

764
00:44:31,752 --> 00:44:35,839
But, I won't let that happen again.

765
00:44:37,424 --> 00:44:41,095
Anyway, Emilia,
you set the press conference.

766
00:44:41,929 --> 00:44:44,682
We'll face the public as one family.

767
00:44:44,890 --> 00:44:48,268
Strong and united.

768
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:51,021
Perfect!

769
00:44:52,272 --> 00:44:53,941
-[Emilia chuckles]
-To the Ardientes.

770
00:45:00,531 --> 00:45:02,116
[Diego] Leave it to me.

771
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:06,662
I'll make sure they'll testify
against the Ardientes.

772
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:09,415
Just be careful, Diego.

773
00:45:10,374 --> 00:45:12,418
And thank you. I appreciate your help.

774
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:15,087
You know I'd do anything for you.

775
00:45:15,587 --> 00:45:19,550
[romantic guitar music playing]

776
00:45:28,725 --> 00:45:29,893
See you, Ivy.

777
00:45:30,310 --> 00:45:31,937
I'll be going, Mrs. Camia.

778
00:45:42,656 --> 00:45:46,869
Lily, I know that our battle
has only just begun.

779
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:50,622
We'll have more challenges to face.

780
00:45:52,499 --> 00:45:54,960
But one day, you'll be happy.

781
00:45:56,336 --> 00:45:57,463
And Diego too.

782
00:46:04,052 --> 00:46:05,387
[phone rings]

783
00:46:09,391 --> 00:46:10,350
Emilia.

784
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:11,351
[Emilia] <i>Hi, Ivy.</i>

785
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:12,853
How are you?

786
00:46:12,936 --> 00:46:15,022
<i>I hope you're well-rested now.</i>

787
00:46:15,105 --> 00:46:16,648
I need your help.

788
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:19,776
[chuckles] Why do you need my help?

789
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:20,736
<i>Well…</i>

790
00:46:20,819 --> 00:46:23,363
We're having a grand press conference
for Papa tomorrow

791
00:46:23,447 --> 00:46:25,699
<i>to fix the mess that, you know…</i>

792
00:46:25,782 --> 00:46:27,326
So I want you to come with me.

793
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:30,454
It's fine with me.

794
00:46:30,537 --> 00:46:34,082
But what about the congressman?
I thought he was mad at me.

795
00:46:34,166 --> 00:46:36,543
Well, my dear, this is the perfect time

796
00:46:36,627 --> 00:46:40,380
for you to fix your mess
with the congressman.

797
00:46:40,464 --> 00:46:42,090
Don't worry, I'll back you up.

798
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:45,177
Good idea. All right, Emilia.
I'll be there.

799
00:46:45,594 --> 00:46:46,762
<i>See you.</i>

800
00:46:46,845 --> 00:46:49,306
Brilliant! Bye, dear, take care.

801
00:46:56,021 --> 00:47:00,567
Mom. I know where you're going
to make your big reveal.

802
00:47:06,698 --> 00:47:09,159
I like that smile, Emilia.

803
00:47:09,993 --> 00:47:13,372
Smile of success, Aunt Claire. Tomorrow,

804
00:47:13,455 --> 00:47:18,126
the crowd will be cheering
the name of Emilia Ardiente.

805
00:47:18,210 --> 00:47:19,044
[chuckles]

806
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:22,965
You know, Auntie, it might even
give Papa a heart attack.

807
00:47:23,048 --> 00:47:26,677
That press conference
will bury him into the ground.

808
00:47:28,720 --> 00:47:30,889
He's in for a big surprise.

809
00:47:32,516 --> 00:47:34,142
That's more like it.

810
00:47:44,486 --> 00:47:46,280
[Emilia] <i>Papa, look who's here!</i>

811
00:47:46,363 --> 00:47:48,198
[Julio] <i>You know,</i>
<i>I was under the impression</i>

812
00:47:48,282 --> 00:47:51,952
<i>you were hiding from me</i>
<i>because you did something wrong.</i>

813
00:47:52,035 --> 00:47:55,414
[Ivy] <i>Is it because I'm one</i>
<i>of your suspects</i>

814
00:47:55,497 --> 00:47:58,333
<i>behind the attacks against you?</i>

815
00:47:58,417 --> 00:48:02,546
[host] <i>Let's welcome the Ardiente Family!</i>

816
00:48:02,629 --> 00:48:05,340
[Emilia] <i>You know, Camia Cruz,</i>
<i>if you're telling the truth,</i>

817
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:07,926
<i>then come out. Show yourself.</i>

818
00:48:08,010 --> 00:48:10,887
[Camia] <i>Well, Emilia? Cat got your tongue?</i>

819
00:48:10,971 --> 00:48:12,723
<i>Or would you prefer this?</i>

820
00:48:12,806 --> 00:48:14,558
<i>Why the long face?</i>

821
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:19,354
[theme music playing]
